message.content:
{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "For the U1 landing page, reuse the existing Spring XD AngularJS UI framework and pre-built navigation components to minimize custom code and ensure consistency with the existing UI design system.",
    "For U2 retry configuration, leverage Spring Retry's built-in exception-based retry policy extension point to add configurable retryable exception lists, and add explicit logic to skip retries for Kryo deserialization failures.",
    "For library updates (U3, U4, U5), use Maven dependency management to bump version numbers, and rely on the existing Spring XD integration test suite to validate compatibility, with no planned changes to public module APIs for these minor/patch version updates.",
    "For U6 module/container id exposure, inject the ids as standard Spring environment properties and OS environment variables, following the existing pattern used for other module-level metadata like the module name.",
    "For U7 Kafka bus property overrides, map new user-facing properties directly to native Spring Kafka consumer and producer configuration options, with deployment-time validation to reject invalid values early.",
    "For U8 RPM script consolidation, structure the single repository with separate top-level directories for base XD RPMs and XD+Ambari RPMs to maintain clear separation of concerns, and update existing CI/CD pipelines to point to the new repository location."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The third-party library updates (Spring Integration 4.1.5, Spring Integration Kafka 1.2.0, Spring Hadoop 2.2.0 GA) have no breaking API changes that require modifications to existing Spring XD module code.",
    "The existing Spring XD UI codebase is built with AngularJS 1.x, which supports adding new views and navigation links without requiring a full UI framework upgrade.",
    "The existing Spring XD Kafka bus implementation is built on Spring Kafka, so the new consumer/producer properties can be mapped directly to native Spring Kafka configuration options without custom implementation work.",
    "The existing RPM build scripts are compatible with being migrated to a single Git repository without requiring changes to the underlying rpmbuild or Maven build tooling configuration.",
    "The Spring XD module runtime already injects standard module metadata (e.g., module name) into the module application context, so adding module id and container id follows the same established injection pattern.",
    "The RabbitMessageBus retry logic is implemented using Spring Retry, so adding configurable retryable exceptions only requires modifying the retry policy configuration, not the core retry execution logic.",
    "The org.springframework.amqp.support.converter.MessageConversionException is available on the classpath when the Rabbit transport is configured, resolving the ClassNotFoundException issue described in U2 by ensuring the correct AMQP library is included in the Rabbit transport classpath."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "U1 Landing Page Design and Analysis",
      "activity_description": "Review existing Spring XD UI navigation structure, design landing page layout with links to sources, processors, sinks, and jobs sections, align with existing UI design patterns and routing logic.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 Landing Page UI Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the new landing page view, create higher-order navigation links, integrate with existing UI routing, add minimal styling to match the existing Spring XD UI look and feel.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2 RabbitMessageBus Retry Configuration Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Add configuration properties for retryable exception lists at both bus and stream deployment level, implement logic to disable retries for Kryo deserialization errors, fix exception class handling to use the correct AMQP MessageConversionException, update the Spring Retry template to use the configured exception list, and add unit tests for the new retry logic.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3 Spring Integration 4.1.5 Update",
      "activity_description": "Update the Maven dependency version for Spring Integration to 4.1.5, run the full Spring XD unit and integration test suite to verify compatibility, and fix any minor compatibility issues that arise (per assumptions, no major breaking changes are expected).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4 Spring Integration Kafka 1.2.0 Update",
      "activity_description": "Update the Maven dependency version for the Spring Integration Kafka extension to 1.2.0, run all Kafka-related integration tests to verify no breaking changes to existing Kafka module functionality.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5 Spring Hadoop 2.2.0 GA Update",
      "activity_description": "Update the Maven dependency version for Spring Hadoop to 2.2.0 GA, run all Hadoop-related integration tests to verify compatibility with existing Hadoop source and sink modules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6 Module and Container ID Exposure Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Add logic to inject module id and container id as Spring environment properties and OS environment variables into all module (source/processor/sink) contexts, and update developer documentation to show how to access these ids for logging purposes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7 Kafka Bus Property Override Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Add new configuration properties for Kafka module consumers (autoCommitEnabled, queueSize, maxWait, fetchSize) and producers (batchSize, batchTimeout) to the Kafka bus configuration class, map these properties to underlying Spring Kafka configuration options, add deployment-time validation for property values, and update documentation for the new properties.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8 RPM Script Consolidation",
      "activity_description": "Create a new single public Git repository with separate top-level directories for base XD RPMs and XD+Ambari RPMs, migrate existing RPM build scripts from the old separate repositories, update CI/CD pipelines to use the new repository location, and verify that RPM builds work correctly for both variants.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "End-to-End Integration Testing",
      "activity_description": "Run the full Spring XD integration test suite to validate all implemented features (landing page, retry configuration, library updates, ID exposure, Kafka properties, RPM builds) and ensure no regressions in existing functionality, fix any issues identified during testing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Documentation Update",
      "activity_description": "Update all relevant user and developer documentation to cover the new features: landing page navigation, RabbitMessageBus retry configuration and exception handling rules, new Kafka bus consumer/producer properties, module/container id access for logging, and the new consolidated RPM repository location.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 32
  }
}

